# Fights at Orerve, a feudal system 6.8 light years from Lave, and meets the Transporter, Boulder, Moray and Krait.
# It starts from combat-orerve.cdr (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the fighter (a military laser, ECM, an energy
# unit, 20 kills) with its random state 5,624,772 draws on. It finds Orerve on the short-range chart and jumps
# there. In space it holds J and full speed whenever no ship but a rock or a barrel is about: while the jump drive
# is engaged, ships of every class spawn 32 times as often (ScaleSpawnOdds) until a ship mass-locks the drive. The
# three combat replays share out the ship types the rest of the corpus does not meet. Between them they meet the
# Boulder, Transporter, Shuttle, Anaconda, Moray, Barrel, Boa, Cobra Mk I, Gecko, Fer-de-Lance, Plate and Escape
# Pod, which no other replay meets; a Cobra Mk III, which elsewhere is only the hull escape-pod abandons; and the
# Krait, Worm and Sidewinder, which hyperspace-and-fight meets too. Their draw counts were found by a search over
# counts for the three runs that meet all sixteen in the least game time. The fight was played by a scratch program
# that steered at the nearest ship by its position each frame and fired when it was in the sights; what it pressed
# is recorded here like any other replay.
file JAMESON.CDR combat-orerve.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # D10, Disc access, on Load commander
key 1; wait 0.3                    # Load commander: the catalogue, JAMESON.CDR selected
key Return; wait 0.5               # loaded
